        "q": "Does elapsedTime on a live workout builder subtract the time a workout spent paused?",
        "a": "No. Apple documents the property as the elapsed time for the workout based on the builder's current contents, including pauses. If your interface promises something like moving time or working time, that is a number you derive rather than one you read. Our advice, offered as judgement: define each clock your product shows in exactly one place in code, drive every screen and every saved summary from that definition, and never let a view compute its own version. Independently computed timers drift, and users notice a mismatch between the ring and the summary long before a test does."
